# M3.5.2 release-manifest self-reference diagnostic — 2026-08-27

## Finding

A manifest cannot both contain the SHA of the commit that contains that same
manifest and be byte-for-byte immutable: committing the generated file changes
the commit SHA. Treating both requirements as simultaneous would create a
circular, unverifiable release contract.

## Resolution

The Control implementation and manifest schema are versioned and merged first
as artifact commit **A**. Only afterward is the manifest generated from the
clean checkout at A and the clean application release. The generated manifest
is stored outside the live Control worktree with mode `0600`; its printed
SHA-256 is the approval/evidence identifier. `control_sha` binds the verifier
implementation at A, not a later evidence commit. A future evidence commit may
record the digest but must not reinterpret `control_sha`.

The release archive must contain the exact application and Control checkouts
named by the manifest. The restore verifier validates both after extraction.
No manifest instance is committed in M3.5.2 because no business-approved
RPO/RTO/retention values or qualifying fresh archive exist.
